#ROOM
Vnum     9000
Name     New Prisoner Processing~
Sector   city~
Desc     A brightly lit processing bay is divided into marked standing positions,
scanner arches and compact administrative terminals. New arrivals are photographed,
searched and entered into the detention network before being transferred deeper into
the secure complex. Every surface is deliberately plain, durable and easy to clean.
~
#EXIT
Direction southeast~
ToRoom    9018
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9001
Name     Earth Penitentiary~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob prototype~
Desc     The public entrance to the Hague detention complex is austere but orderly.
Reinforced composite walls frame security doors, visitor information displays and
a staffed reception point beneath the seal of the Terran authorities. Secure routes
lead toward prisoner processing and visitor screening, while a municipal training
annex occupies a separate public wing.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    398
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9034
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southeast~
ToRoom    9003
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southwest~
ToRoom    9002
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9002
Name     Prisoner Entrance~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This controlled entrance is reserved for prisoners, escorts and secure
transports. Heavy doors, floor markings and recessed surveillance units funnel each
arrival toward the first checkpoint. Beyond the public entrance, the atmosphere
changes immediately from civic administration to tightly managed custody.
~
#EXIT
Direction northeast~
ToRoom    9001
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southwest~
ToRoom    9004
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9003
Name     Visitor Entrance~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Visitors enter through a separate screening corridor lined with identity
scanners, prohibited-item notices and secure storage lockers. Clear panels allow
staff to observe the route without giving visitors any view into restricted parts
of the prison. The passage continues toward the visitors checkpoint.
~
#EXIT
Direction northwest~
ToRoom    9001
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southeast~
ToRoom    9017
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9004
Name     Outside Checkpoint A~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     A reinforced security door blocks the way south. Cameras cover every angle
of the narrow approach while a wall display instructs escorts to present custody
credentials before proceeding. The checkpoint is designed to prevent an arriving
prisoner from reaching the secure interior without positive authorization.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9005
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction northeast~
ToRoom    9002
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 9004 2 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9005
Name     Inside Checkpoint A~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The inner side of Checkpoint A forms a compact security vestibule between
independently controlled doors. Status lights show the outer barrier sealed before
the route south can be cleared. Reinforced walls and ceiling-mounted sensors make
this space intentionally difficult to bypass or damage.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9004
Flags     isdoor closed locked~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9006
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 9005 0 2
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9006
Name     A Prison Corridor~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     A broad institutional corridor runs through the processing wing. Pale wall
panels, anti-slip flooring and continuous lighting leave few shadows, while sealed
service conduits disappear behind tamper-resistant access plates. Surveillance
cameras track movement between the nearby checkpoints and staff station.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9005
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9009
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9007
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9007
Name     Outside Check Point B~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Checkpoint B divides prisoner processing from the main secure circulation
route. A pair of recessed scanners flank the southern doorway and a red status band
runs around the frame whenever access is denied. There is nowhere to wait except
inside the direct view of the facility's cameras.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9006
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9008
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9008
Name     Inside Check Point B~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The inner checkpoint opens onto the prison's controlled circulation network.
Directional markings identify processing, accommodation and staff-only routes, and
a ceiling strip displays current lockdown status. The construction is functional,
severe and clearly intended to survive years of hard institutional use.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9007
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9000
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southeast~
ToRoom    9010
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9009
Name     Staff Check Point~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This staff checkpoint is little more than a hardened control alcove built
into the corridor wall. Secure terminals display camera feeds, door states and
prisoner movements while lockers hold emergency equipment. Access beyond the station
is intended for authorized detention personnel only.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9006
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9010
Name     A Prison Corridor~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The corridor angles through the secure interior beneath evenly spaced light
panels. Numbered door markings and discreet floor guides replace decoration, and the
quiet hum of ventilation is broken only by distant doors opening and sealing again.
Every junction remains under visible surveillance.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9011
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction northwest~
ToRoom    9008
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9011
Name     Outside Checkpoint C~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     A third controlled checkpoint stands at a junction leading toward the cell
and service wings. The doorway is framed by identification sensors and hardened
shutters capable of sealing the passage during an incident. Floor markings keep
staff traffic separated from escorted prisoners.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9012
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9020
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9010
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9012
Name     A Prison Corridor~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This narrower corridor leads toward the visitor-control section. Smooth
composite walls contain no exposed fixtures beyond lights, cameras and emergency
call points. The air carries the faint antiseptic smell common to the rest of the
facility.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9011
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction northeast~
ToRoom    9013
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9013
Name     Viewing Room Checkpoint~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Visitors and prisoners are separated here before entering the controlled
visitation suite. Identity readers, a small guard console and a secure intercom are
built into the wall. Beyond the checkpoint, reinforced observation glazing ensures
that contact can be monitored without compromising the secure perimeter.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9014
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction southwest~
ToRoom    9012
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9014
Name     Viewing Room~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     A row of fixed seats faces a broad panel of reinforced transparent composite.
The adjoining visiting room can be seen clearly through it, while directional audio
and recording systems allow conversations to be monitored. Nothing in the room is
loose enough to be removed or used as a weapon.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9015
Flags     window~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9013
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9015
Name     Visiting Room~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The visiting room contains fixed tables and chairs arranged beneath bright,
neutral lighting. Reinforced glazing separates portions of the suite, and unobtrusive
cameras cover every seat. The space is less severe than the cell blocks, but every
detail still makes its custodial purpose unmistakable.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9016
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9014
Flags     window~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9016
Name     Inside Visitors Checkpoint~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This secure vestibule controls movement between the visiting suite and the
public side of the complex. Staff can isolate either doorway from a recessed console,
and a narrow inspection strip in the wall provides a clear view of anyone waiting
to pass through.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9017
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9015
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9017
Name     Outside Visitors Checkpoint~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The public side of the visitors checkpoint contains queue markings, identity
terminals and lockers for restricted belongings. Posted notices explain visitation
rules in several common languages. A controlled passage south leads into the secure
visiting suite.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9016
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction northwest~
ToRoom    9003
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9018
Name     Strip Search~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Privacy screens divide this stark search room into several inspection bays.
Wall lockers hold scanners, gloves and sealed evidence containers, while floor drains
and washable surfaces make the room easy to sanitize. Prisoners are searched here
before being issued detention clothing.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9019
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9019
Name     Prison Garments~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Shelving units hold standardized detention clothing, footwear and sealed
personal-property bags. Each set is tagged to a prisoner record before issue, and a
small return chute carries civilian belongings into secure storage elsewhere in the
complex.
~
#EXIT
Direction northeast~
ToRoom    9010
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9020
Name     Inside Checkpoint C~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Beyond Checkpoint C, the architecture becomes more restrictive. Heavy doors
sit flush with reinforced walls and the floor is marked with routes toward housing,
visitation and dining. A status panel overhead can turn the entire junction into a
sealed containment point within seconds.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9011
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9021
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9021
Name     A Prison Corridor~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This main corridor serves the accommodation and dining sections. Recessed
lights cast an even white glow over doors, cameras and numbered wall panels. The
smell of institutional food drifts faintly from the east while the cell blocks lie
further south.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9020
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9030
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9022
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9022
Name     A Prison Corridor~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The corridor continues toward the cell-block checkpoints beneath the constant
hum of filtered air. Directional numbers are stencilled directly onto the wall panels,
and every few metres a recessed emergency station sits behind a sealed cover.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9021
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9023
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9023
Name     A Prison Corridor~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The passage reaches a controlled junction between two cell-block approaches.
Reinforced doors stand east and west, each watched by independent camera clusters.
The open route north leads back toward the service and dining sections of the complex.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9022
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9024
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9025
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9024
Name     CellBlock Checkpoint~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This checkpoint controls entry to Cellblock A. A compact guard station is
protected behind reinforced transparent composite, with door controls and prisoner
movement records displayed on its internal screens. The heavy eastern barrier leads
into the housing block itself.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9026
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9023
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9025
Name     CellBlock Checkpoint~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     A second cell-block checkpoint occupies the western branch of the junction.
Its reinforced access door is presently inactive, but the camera housings, security
console and emergency shutters remain operational. The main prison corridor lies back
to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9023
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9026
Name     Cellblock A~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Cellblock A is built around a stark central passage with sealed cell doors
set into reinforced walls. Numbers and status lights identify each compartment while
ceiling cameras watch the entire block. The hard surfaces amplify footsteps and the
metallic sound of doors cycling open and shut.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9029
Keywords  Cell~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9027
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9024
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9027
Name     Cellblock A~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The cellblock passage continues between identical reinforced doors and narrow
inspection panels. A continuous strip of white light follows the ceiling while the
walls carry only cell numbers, emergency instructions and the occasional maintenance
access plate.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9028
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9026
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9028
Name     Cellblock A~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     This end of Cellblock A terminates in a blank reinforced wall beneath a pair
of surveillance cameras. The cell doors here are spaced closely together, each with
a small status panel showing occupancy and lock state. The only open route returns
west along the block.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9027
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9029
Name     A Cell~
Sector   city~
Flags    safe hotel prototype~
Desc     A narrow detention cell contains a fixed bunk, compact sanitation unit and a
small recessed shelf. The furnishings are moulded or anchored directly into the room,
leaving almost nothing loose. A reinforced door separates the cell from Cellblock A.

You may safely quit and reenter the game from here.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9026
Keywords  Cell~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9030
Name     Outside the Dining Area~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     The prison corridor widens outside the dining section. Painted queue lines
lead north toward the main room while a secured service route runs east toward the
kitchen. The smell of hot nutrient rations and cleaning agents hangs in the air.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9031
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9033
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9021
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9031
Name     Prison Dining Room~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Rows of fixed tables and benches fill this supervised dining room. The
furniture is rounded, heavy and bolted to the floor, with clear sightlines from every
seat to the entrances. A service opening to the east connects the room to the food
line while cameras watch from the ceiling corners.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    9032
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9030
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9032
Name     Food Line~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     A stainless serving counter separates prisoners from the kitchen beyond.
Heated dispensers issue standardized meals in sealed trays, and floor markings keep
the queue moving in a single direction. The equipment is designed for speed,
hygiene and minimal physical contact between staff and inmates.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    9033
Flags     window~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9031
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 9002 1 9032
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9033
Name     The Prison Kitchen~
Sector   city~
Flags    prototype~
Desc     Industrial cookers, chilled storage units and sealed preparation benches fill
this compact institutional kitchen. Everything is arranged for high-volume meals and
easy sanitation. A secure serving window opens north toward the food line, while the
western door leads back to the controlled dining corridor.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    9032
Flags     window~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9030
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 9001 1 9033
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     9034
Name     Hague Public Training Centre~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This municipal training centre provides basic physical, cognitive and social
conditioning for residents, academy students and public-service personnel. Six
standardized training stations line the room beneath simple instructional displays.
The equipment is deliberately practical rather than elite, providing a reliable
place to TRAIN an attribute before seeking more specialized facilities elsewhere.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    9001
#ENDEXIT

